From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: light.msstyles: a Dark colour scheme

The Light visual style gains a second colour scheme, "Dark", beside "Blue"
(Stained Glass Light), as a Windows style carries several: COLORNAMES,
FILERESNAMES and the display names list it, and DARK_INI plus its dark_*.bmp
images come from dark.rc, which wine-sg's theme/dark.py generates from
BLUE_INI and the rendered Light images when build.sh prepares the tree --
so Dark follows every change to Light and nothing is drawn twice.

Blue's [SysMetrics] colours are now the Stained Glass Light palette (sg-shell
theme/50-sg-colors.reg: white captions, the purple accent), so switching back
from Dark lands where a new profile starts rather than on Wine's blue
captions.

Gate: test/darkmode-gate.sh (with 0161-0163).
---
--- a/dlls/light.msstyles/light.rc
+++ b/dlls/light.msstyles/light.rc
@@ -26,12 +26,14 @@
 STRINGTABLE
 {
     IDS_COLOR_DISPLAY_NAME_BLUE         "Blue"
+    IDS_COLOR_DISPLAY_NAME_DARK         "Dark"
 }
 
 /* Theme color tooltips */
 STRINGTABLE
 {
     IDS_COLOR_TOOLTIP_BLUE         "Blue"
+    IDS_COLOR_TOOLTIP_DARK         "Dark"
 }
 
 /* Theme size display names */
@@ -55,6 +57,7 @@
 1 COLORNAMES
 {
 "Blue\0"
+"Dark\0"
 "\0"
 }
 
@@ -69,6 +72,7 @@
